# Day 25 – FULL JOIN

## What I Learned
Today I learned about:

- FULL JOIN → combines LEFT JOIN and RIGHT JOIN
- How to show all matched and unmatched data
- When FULL JOIN is useful in data analysis

FULL JOIN returns all rows from both tables.

---

## What is FULL JOIN?

FULL JOIN returns:

- All rows from the left table
- All rows from the right table
- Matching rows are combined
- Non-matching rows show NULL on the missing side

---

## Simple Rule

FULL JOIN = Keep everything from BOTH tables

---

## FULL JOIN Syntax

```sql
SELECT column_name
FROM table1
FULL JOIN table2
ON table1.column_name = table2.column_name;
